{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "No supported optimization can be applied without risking coverage loss or violating unverified prerequisites. The build job runs 20 independent SDK/xcode matrix combinations; enabling fail-fast (P-LIT-FAIL-FAST) would cancel remaining builds after one failure, losing build coverage across SDKs, and required_checks is not_verified so we cannot confirm every matrix outcome is dispensable. There is no explicit dependency installation step in the workflow to cache (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE); the job checks out and runs xcodebuild directly, so there is no measurable repeated dependency fetch to target. No representative successful-duration history is available (ci_history is historical_context_only with no durations), so a custom timeout (P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT) cannot be safely bounded. The workflow is push/PR/dispatch-driven with no scheduled runs, so schedule-suppression patterns (P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE, P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE) do not apply. Test selection/prioritization (P-LIT-SELECT, P-LIT-PRIORITIZE) would reduce the single test job's coverage, which the workflow already marks advisory but still intends to run.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-FAIL-SCHEDULE", "P-LIT-IDLE-SCHEDULE", "P-LIT-SELECT", "P-LIT-PRIORITIZE"]
}
